26
00:01:18,060 --> 00:01:20,340
Now, let's go back
to LLM agents.

27
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:24,070
So the code of a large
language model based agent

28
00:01:24,070 --> 00:01:29,070
is that the brain of this agent
is a large language model, which

29
00:01:29,070 --> 00:01:32,970
is going to perform reasoning
and planning to take action

30
00:01:32,970 --> 00:01:34,390
at each time step.

31
00:01:34,390 --> 00:01:38,110
Then with this action to
interact with the environment,

32
00:01:38,110 --> 00:01:42,300
it will receive the feedback
and revise its internal memory

33
00:01:42,300 --> 00:01:46,050
so that it can better plan
for the next step to take.

34
00:01:46,050 --> 00:01:48,400
So with this [? text ?]
agent framework,

35
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:51,870
it allows the LLM to also
utilize this external feedback

36
00:01:51,870 --> 00:01:55,020
and tools whenever available,
so that it can further

37
00:01:55,020 --> 00:01:57,770
expand its capability
and to give

38
00:01:57,770 --> 00:02:02,400
to get more informed decision in
its own decision making process.

39
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:05,390
So some common components
in the agent framework

40
00:02:05,390 --> 00:02:08,240
include tool use and retrieval.

41
00:02:08,240 --> 00:02:10,820
Then why do you want to empower
these large language models

42
00:02:10,820 --> 00:02:12,920
with the agent framework?

43
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:15,410
Because solving real
world tasks typically

44
00:02:15,410 --> 00:02:18,320
involves a trial
and error process,

45
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:23,070
especially when we deploy this
LLM agent in a new environment.

46
00:02:23,070 --> 00:02:26,330
It really needs to interact
with the environment

47
00:02:26,330 --> 00:02:28,790
to understand some
success and failure

48
00:02:28,790 --> 00:02:32,630
modes in different actions
so that it is able to revise

49
00:02:32,630 --> 00:02:34,670
its own internal memory.

50
00:02:34,670 --> 00:02:37,490
At the same time,
leveraging external tools

51
00:02:37,490 --> 00:02:40,910
and retrieving from external
knowledge for expanded LLM

52
00:02:40,910 --> 00:02:42,800
capabilities.

53
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:44,810
And with the more like--

54
00:02:44,810 --> 00:02:47,940
with this agent, your workflow
design becomes more mature.

55
00:02:47,940 --> 00:02:52,440
It also facilitates the
accomplishment of complex tasks.

56
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:55,260
This includes tasks
decomposition,

57
00:02:55,260 --> 00:03:00,570
allocation of subtasks, division
of labor for collaboration

58
00:03:00,570 --> 00:03:02,640
between different
specialized modules

59
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:06,870
and multi-agent generation.

60
00:03:06,870 --> 00:03:10,770
Many people are saying
that this year, 2025,

61
00:03:10,770 --> 00:03:13,620
will be the year of agents.

62
00:03:13,620 --> 00:03:16,950
Nowadays, we have already
seen explosion of LLM agents

63
00:03:16,950 --> 00:03:18,870
for various applications.

64
00:03:18,870 --> 00:03:21,330
And in many domains,
actually, these agents

65
00:03:21,330 --> 00:03:25,740
transformed how previous people
are thinking about all these AI

66
00:03:25,740 --> 00:03:28,290
models can-- how these
AI models can behave.

67
00:03:28,290 --> 00:03:31,390
So some very successful
demonstrations

68
00:03:31,390 --> 00:03:34,990
and also practical use cases
include code generation,

69
00:03:34,990 --> 00:03:38,680
computer use, personal
assistant and robotics.

70
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:43,380
And this list of applications
will keep growing in the future

71
00:03:43,380 --> 00:03:43,900
as well.

72
00:03:43,900 --> 00:03:47,390
And also there are some domains
like education, finance, et

73
00:03:47,390 --> 00:03:50,970
cetera, where we already have
seen an emergence of a pretty

74
00:03:50,970 --> 00:03:52,510
nice LLM-based agents.

75
00:03:52,510 --> 00:03:56,150
Another factor that further
drives this excitement about LLM

76
00:03:56,150 --> 00:03:59,600
agent development is about
this recent rapid progress

77
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:03,350
of reasoning models, starting
from September last year

78
00:04:03,350 --> 00:04:08,160
with the release of OpenAI o1
And starting from that model,

79
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:12,830
we have also seen a lot of
great reasoning progress

80
00:04:12,830 --> 00:04:13,860
during the meantime.

81
00:04:13,860 --> 00:04:16,610
For example, last month
we saw the release

82
00:04:16,610 --> 00:04:20,390
of the Gemini 2.0 Flash
Thinking model and also

83
00:04:20,390 --> 00:04:21,959
